[33m97854fd[m D. "Full Fledge App" Enhancements (Postpone or Simplify for "Free & Offline"): Real Backend & Database (Postpone Indefinitely for "Completely Free"): Firebase Firestore/Storage on a free ("Spark") plan has limits. If you exceed them, you'll incur costs. Sticking to localStorage and IndexedDB for primary data storage aligns with your "completely free" and "offline" goals. Exception: Firebase Authentication (Google Sign-In) free tier is generous for auth itself. Firestore for role detection only (a very small amount of data per user) is likely fine on the free tier. User Account Management & Teacher Approval Flow (Simplify): The single NEXT_PUBLIC_TEACHER_EMAIL and offline debug login are good starting points. If you need more teachers, they'd have to manually configure their NEXT_PUBLIC_TEACHER_EMAIL in their own PWA instance, or you'd manage roles in Firestore (minimal data). Actual File Uploads for Assignments (Highly Challenging without Costs): Storing user-uploaded files reliably for free is difficult. Alternatives: Students submit text. Students are instructed to use their own cloud storage (Google Drive, etc.) and submit a link (if the assignment system needs to track it). For a fully offline PWA, file uploads are not directly possible in a way that the "teacher" instance of the PWA can easily access without a server. Telemetry Collection System (Postpone or Use PWA Analytics): Server-side telemetry has costs. You can get some PWA usage analytics via browser developer tools or very basic client-side event logging to localStorage for your own insights if needed.
